        "read": true,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>We are very confused as to how Blazing Tornado works.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>1. When it enters play, it immediately spawns the tornado and the 6 spaces around it are hazard spaces, correct?</p><p>2. How do you mark the hazard spaces? (or do you just know that they are hazardous cause they are adjacent to the tornado?)</p><p>3. If someone is standing adjacent to (or on the space) that the tornado spawns, are they attacked immediately? or not until the end of their next turn (when hazard spaces activate).</p><p>4. If you choose BT as one of your starting power cards, does it spawn immediately during setup?</p><p>5. What happens if you replace BT with another card, does the tornado disappear and, does it then reappear when you put it back into play?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Some of these questions may be really dumb, but I just want to be absolutely clear as to how it works.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "actions_summary": [],
        "moderator": false,
        "admin": false,
        "staff": false,
        "user_id": 334,
        "hidden": false,
        "trust_level": 1,
        "deleted_at": null,
        "user_deleted": false,
        "edit_reason": null,
        "can_view_edit_history": true,
        "wiki": false,
        "can_accept_answer": false,
        "can_unaccept_answer": false,
        "accepted_answer": false,
        "topic_accepted_answer": false
      },
      {
        "id": 114710,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-15T00:55:01.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>1. Correct.</p><p>2. You just know because it's next to and on the Tornado.</p><p>3. No, they did not enter the Hazard Space, so they are not instantly attacked. They will not be attacked until the move onto a Hazard Space or end their turn on it.</p><p>4. Yes.</p><p>5. It disappears when the card leaves play. If you play Blazing Tornado again later (note you cannot remove it and play it again on the same turn) it will once again be placed somewhere in Ra's current Line of SIght.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:46:41.443Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
