      {
        "id": 114712,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-15T01:03:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>1,4&amp;5. &nbsp;Blazing Tornado enters play when the card enters play, so you can spawn with it. &nbsp;(really great map control to start) &nbsp;If you swap out Blazing tornado, or the card leaves play the tornado goes away. &nbsp;It comes back when the card is played, once again anywhere in Ra's line of sight. &nbsp;As soon as it enters play the hazard spaces are active.</p><p>2. &nbsp;Hazard spaces are unmarked, just have to remember to check what cards are in play, and remember that Tornado will burn you.</p><p>3. &nbsp;No. &nbsp;Only when they enter a hazard space or end their turn on it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Tornado is mostly map control, it is great for stopping Vis or Unity from hiding out in advantageous places. &nbsp;It also is great for melting AZ's Structures.</p><p>Spawning it on someone would seem to be legal. &nbsp;I can't remember if that was a thing.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:46:41.583Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.2,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 10968,
