        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>1,4&amp;5. &nbsp;Blazing Tornado enters play when the card enters play, so you can spawn with it. &nbsp;(really great map control to start) &nbsp;If you swap out Blazing tornado, or the card leaves play the tornado goes away. &nbsp;It comes back when the card is played, once again anywhere in Ra&#39;s line of sight. &nbsp;As soon as it enters play the hazard spaces are active.</p><p>2. &nbsp;Hazard spaces are unmarked, just have to remember to check what cards are in play, and remember that Tornado will burn you.</p><p>3. &nbsp;No. &nbsp;Only when they enter a hazard space or end their turn on it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Tornado is mostly map control, it is great for stopping Vis or Unity from hiding out in advantageous places. &nbsp;It also is great for melting AZ&#39;s Structures.</p><p>Spawning it on someone would seem to be legal. &nbsp;I can&#39;t remember if that was a thing.</p>",
